# Project articles in Assets (20 October 2026)

- A project explicitly declares `article = {fileId,title,sha256,thumbnailUrl}`. Article precedes Files in Classic and Tube; projects without this declaration keep their existing default. A manual thumbnail remains an explicit override. The catalogue transports a bounded raster thumbnail of the real article opening and its reference, never the HTML. (20 October 2026)
- `ProjectArticle.jsx` reads only the selected file. `assetsProjectArticle.js` removes active markup, injects a restrictive content policy and renders an iframe without scripts or application-origin access. Native details, internal anchors and HTTPS links remain available. Missing, empty, oversized and failed reads expose an error and retry. (20 October 2026)
- Local reading calls `preview-text` with `format=html`, for inventoried `.html` or `.htm` files up to 32 MiB. Ordinary text keeps its 256 KiB cap. Cloud reading reuses `resolveEntryBytes`; a transient local failure can fall back to an existing archive. Documents must embed their fonts and illustrations. (20 October 2026)
- `set-article` validates the metadata, reads the actual inventoried HTML and checks its reviewed SHA-256. It locks `Projects.json`, rereads the current record and updates only its article reference, preserving independent changes to sources and other fields. Normal archive publication subsequently carries that reference to the compact catalogue. (20 October 2026)
- Authoring and filing belong to `/Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-edit/references/ProjectArticles.md`. The renderer takes editable JSON and an exact dependency manifest. Filing requires the registered project identity; publication requires the reviewed HTML hash. Queued archive jobs do not establish cloud completeness. (20 October 2026)
- UV-Match Height remains under the registered workshop's excluded `Drafts/Article/` until review. Defer canonical skill filing too: `com.zenray.skills-sync` mirrors canonical skills every 60 seconds into watched Memory independently of the filing command. Do not modify that global service. (20 October 2026)
- Delivery after approval: reconcile the branch with current origin/main, run the affected checks and build, deploy the application, safely reload the Assets daemon, then run the approved filing command. Inspect both target-project and zenray-edit archive jobs and exact file receipts before reporting cloud backup. No deployment or article publication occurs in the preparation phase. (20 October 2026)
- Checks: `npm test -- scripts/AssetsService.test.js src/components/assets src/lib/assetsProjectArticle.test.js src/lib/assetsWorkspaceCatalogue.test.js src/lib/assetsWorkspaceViewModel.test.js src/lib/assetsWorkspaceBridge.test.js scripts/AssetsCloudPublisher.test.js scripts/AssetsPublishTransaction.test.js --maxWorkers=1`; `npm run build`; canonical edit `node --test scripts/file-article.test.mjs`. The workshop verifier uses the real component, with its API writer disabled, to exercise both layouts and HTML isolation. (20 October 2026)

## Ton neutre court and article contents (20 October 2026)

- Project articles use factual, descriptive and short explanations, without rhetorical flourishes or editorial commentary. Prompt text remains verbatim. The writing rules are recorded in the article itself and in the canonical zenray-edit method. (20 October 2026)
- The left contents sidebar can be pinned, detached or hidden. Pinning reserves space beside the document; narrow frames start with a closed, independently controlled drawer. Native HTML controls require no scripts. (20 October 2026)
- Internal links inside srcdoc must use about:srcdoc#section; bare fragments inherit the parent document URL. The reader transforms only declared fragment links, preserving its content policy and isolated origin. (20 October 2026)
